## 📝 Executive Summary
The **Sterling Ridge Enterprise Network Portfolio** models a robust three-site enterprise infrastructure consisting of:
* **New York (HQ):** Hosts HR, Operations, and IT users.
* **Georgia (Branch):** Hosts Sales and Marketing teams.
* **Texas (Data Center):** Houses IT departments and a server farm hosting critical infrastructure (DNS, Web/FTP, and public file services).

Each site utilizes a **Cisco 2911 WAN router**, a **3560-series multilayer distribution switch**, and **2960-series access switches** per department, demonstrating a sound, textbook three-tier-lite hierarchical design. 

This review captures the live project configurations, baseline security hygiene (SSH-only management, timeouts, banner protection), and logs the successful remediation of critical connectivity defects—including site-to-site WAN failures and an OSPF router-id collision discovered during live troubleshooting.

